<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21219] ksocklnd: positive EALREADY after retry cap crashes node</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21219</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;After SOCKNAL_MAX_RETRIES refused connects, ksocknal_connect() fails with rc = +EALREADY and completes the queued txs with that positive status. lnet_ping() returns it as a NID count, and lnet_ping_show_dump() dereferences NULL:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000001
RIP: lnet_ping_show_dump+0x3dc
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduced 3/3 by sanity-lnet test_239 on a tree without the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21218" title="ksocklnd: stuck outgoing connect locks the peer out" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21218"&gt;LU-21218&lt;/a&gt; fix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fixes: d4c52652c357 ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19225" title="Limit socklnd connection retries to some sane number" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19225"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19225&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; socklnd: cap the number of retries")&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fix:&lt;/b&gt; use -EALREADY when failing; lnet_ping() returns only negative errors.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
